six('def-quiver-hall-positive-borel','Definition: for no vertices the generator set is empty and the Borel is the coefficient field.|Definition: degree zero contains the torus and unit; it is not the zero algebra.|Definition: one loopless vertex has Cartan entry 2 and no pairwise Serre relations.|Definition: q is a prime power ≥2, so ν>1; no q=1 specialization is claimed.|-The vertex set has no interval endpoints; source/target of an arrow are incidence data.|Definition: the finite vertex/arrow data and numerical ν are fixed; writing generators entails no arbitrary family of choices.')
